# This project follows the DevSecOps template

The plan for this project is my DevSecOps template. **Read it from the
source, not from memory:**

- In this project folder: `./devsecops-template/` (a symlink to the one real copy at `~/orca/projects/devsecops/`; edits there are edits to the real repo)
- Public: https://github.com/nazmur96/devsecops-template
- Start at `README.md` (overview), then `template/README.md` (phase map,
  decisions, "Come back later" table, "Scale the template"), then the phase
  file you're working on (`template/00-…12-*.md`), and `PRACTICE-APPS.md`
  for which app comes next
- Reference files: `template/COMMON-MISTAKES.md`,
  `template/DAY-2-OPERATIONS.md`, `template/WHEN-IT-ALL-RUNS-TOGETHER.md`

## How to work

1. Phases in order, 0 → 11 (12 is later). Before each phase, read its file and
   its section in `COMMON-MISTAKES.md`. A phase is done only when its
   **Prove it** drill has actually run.
2. ⏸ tickets wait for a later phase (template README, "Come back later").
3. Getting the code: open-source apps are **forked, then the fork is cloned**,
   and made safe before the first push (Actions off, read-only token):
   template P1-0. Company repos are cloned directly.
4. Three repos per project: the app repo, `<app>-gitops`, and `platform`
   (Terraform). They sit side by side in this project folder. Tools come from
   each repo's `mise.toml`; **nothing project-specific is installed on the
   host** (NixOS workstation).
5. **AWS:** SSO profile only, never access keys. Budget alert (P0-7) before
   anything is created. **Ask before any action that creates billed AWS
   resources, and before every `terraform apply`/`destroy`.** Destroy at the
   end of every session.
6. **Git:** every change to the project repos goes branch → PR → squash-merge.
   Claude may be working in the same checkouts at the same time, so build each
   PR in **your own `git worktree`** (`git worktree add <dir> -b <branch>
   origin/<default>`), stage files **by name** (never `git add -A`), and check
   `git branch --show-current` right before committing. Worktrees share
   branches: never delete a branch another worktree has checked out. Never
   run `devpod up` in a worktree (its `.git` is a pointer the container
   can't follow); dev containers come from a normal clone.
7. **The template is under test.** When a step is wrong or missing, say so,
   fix it in `~/orca/projects/devsecops` (commit + push to `main`), and add
   an RCA note in this project's `docs/rca/`.
